Moebius Polargraph uses more than one license. This file describes
scope. It does not relicense third-party material.

This project is open source. The complete repository is not uniformly
MIT-licensed.

## Firmware (MIT)

Original firmware contributions and modifications by Lina Lopes, and
derived Walldraw portions, are licensed under the MIT License.

Copyright (c) 2021 shihaipeng03
Copyright (c) 2026 Lina Lopes

The full MIT License text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

This MIT grant covers the Arduino sketches under firmware/ that carry
an SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT header. It does not cover bundled
third-party libraries.

Upstream Walldraw:

  https://github.com/shihaipeng03/Walldraw

Lina Lopes did not create the original Walldraw firmware or hardware.

Moebius_Polargraph_TwoStepperTest.ino is MIT-licensed as source, but it
depends on AccelStepper. AccelStepper is licensed GPL V2 or Commercial
and is not relicensed by the MIT grant. Distributing a combined program
built with AccelStepper is subject to AccelStepper's license terms.

## Original documentation (CC BY 4.0)

Original documentation written by Lina Lopes for Moebius Polargraph is
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(CC BY 4.0).

Canonical deed:

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Full license text:

  LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

This includes README.md, CREDITS.md, LICENSE (this file),
LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY.md, future original manuals written by Lina Lopes,
and original explanatory diagrams and photographs unless a file is
explicitly marked otherwise.

## Future original fabrication files (not applied yet)

No original fabrication files by Lina Lopes are in this repository.
CERN-OHL-S-2.0 is the intended future license for those files when they
exist. It is not applied now and does not cover upstream or third-party
parts.

Intended future license:

  CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 – Strongly Reciprocal
  (CERN-OHL-S-2.0)

## Third-party material (not licensed by Lina Lopes)

Bundled libraries, the 2020 assembly PDF, and other third-party files
keep their original copyrights and licenses. They are listed in
LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY.md.

The 2020 PDF is excluded from the MIT, CC BY 4.0, and future
CERN-OHL-S-2.0 grants described above.
